 "captions": [
  {
   "t": "Why does everything cost nine ninety-nine… and not ten dollars?",
   "s": 0.05,
   "e": 3.07
  },
  {
   "t": "Because your brain reads prices from left to right. Nine ninety-nine feels like nine dollars. Not ten.",
   "s": 3.27,
   "e": 8.79
  },
  {
   "t": "Researchers from MIT and the University of Chicago tested the same item at three prices: thirty-four, thirty-nine and forty-four dollars.",
   "s": 8.99,
   "e": 17.31
  },
  {
   "t": "Which one sold the most? The thirty-nine dollar one. It beat both… even the cheaper price.",
   "s": 17.51,
   "e": 22.62
  },
  {
   "t": "It's called charm pricing. And this Black Friday, it's on almost every tag you'll see.",
   "s": 22.82,
